    "description": "I have extensive experience in systems-level programming, primarily C and C++ and debugging (with modest initial exposure to C# and .NET Framework development), primarily on Windows platforms.  I was initially hired to maintain, port and enhance a custom application-networking protocol layered on top of UDP (and IPX) which continues to function for our Electronic Health Record today.  Designed and developed a high-speed inter-server communication architecture for our custom-desgined in-house EHR database technology.  Played a key role in designing and supporting upgrades the client-server application communication technologies to include XML-over-HTTP services architecture, and also WCF services architecture.  I have also managed email security systems, assist with server administration and troubleshooting when needed, with desktop and end-user support as needed, and serve as a key technical reference for other staff.\n\nI act as a key member of our troubleshooting and incident \"Tiger Teams\", both in actively troubleshooting and determining who else to pull in to help.  Widely recognized as a leaded in teamwork and technical skill, my goal is to link disparate teams and serve as an example of shared problem-solving. \n\nFor the last few years, my focus has been much more on Cyber-Security Analysis and Defense.  In addition to helping stabilize multiple aspects of our practice, I function as a liaison between Security and the Development teams at MCHS, seeking to represent the needs of each to the other, and to enhance communication.",
